# guard-cap-baseline (T-3644) — the DP-3 guard cap, frozen 2026-11-01
#
# Adopted purpose DP-3 (operator 2026-10-29: A; T-3612 draft v0.9 section 5 DP-3 and 6.7):
# guards are capped at 34 canary cron jobs and 99 scripts/check-*.sh. One in, one out.
# Enforced by scripts/check-guard-severity-markers.sh (no new check script: that would
# itself break the cap). It fails naming any scripts/check-*.sh or .context/cron/*.crontab
# that is not listed here, and fails if this file lists more than a cap allows.
#
# To add a guard: retire one in the SAME commit — delete its file and its line here, then
# add the newcomer's line. See docs/operations/guard-layer-and-canaries.md "Guard cap".
#
# Line kinds:
#   cap <kind> <N>         the cap for that kind
#   check <path>           a counted scripts/check-*.sh
#   canary <path>          a counted canary cron job (.context/cron/*.crontab)
#   operational <path>     an operational cron job (supervisor, rollup, re-mint, heartbeat,
#                          audit, sweep): listed so a new crontab must be classified, NOT
#                          counted (DP-3 excludes the 12 operational crons). Fixture suites
#                          (tests/*fixtures*.sh) are not guards and are not listed.
cap check 99
cap canary 34
